    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Kostya approaches Viktor's table to try and swap the poisoned cognac bottle back. Viktor gets angry and tells him to go away. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извините, приятного вам вечера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что тебе нужно от меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне нужна эта бутылка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "О чём ты говоришь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я возьму эту бутылку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А вам поставлю другую.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тебе что, совсем нечего делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, я просто хочу дать другую.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Не трогай ничего, иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но я должен её забрать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я сказал, иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятно, давай дальше.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извините, приятного вам вечера.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excuse me, have a pleasant evening.' Kostya uses the polite plural 'you' here alongside 'sorry', keeping a formal or respectful tone.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Что тебе нужно от меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What do you need from me?' Russian expresses this impersonally, literally saying 'to me' or 'to you' with 'me'. Then Kostya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне нужна эта бутылка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I need this bottle.' Here 'to me' sets up the idea, while 'bottle' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "О чём ты говоришь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you talking about?' Listen for the word meaning 'what' right alongside 'you' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я возьму эту бутылку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will take this bottle.' In Russian, 'I' leads into 'a bottle' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А вам поставлю другую.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I will put another one for you.' Kostya starts with 'you' and pairs it with 'will set' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тебе что, совсем нечего делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you have absolutely nothing to do?' The first content word means 'for you', and 'do' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, я просто хочу дать другую.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, I just want to give another one.' The key word here means 'I', which Kostya combines with 'just'. Chef Viktor answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Не трогай ничего, иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do not touch anything, get out of here!' Here 'touch' sets up the idea, while 'from here' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но я должен её забрать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But I must take it.' You'll hear 'I' all the time in the show, here connected with 'take'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я сказал, иди отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I said, get out of here!' In Russian, 'I' leads into 'from here' in a very natural everyday phrasing. Then Kostya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятно, давай дальше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
